1
00:01:09,350 --> 00:01:14,770
[Connecting to You]

2
00:01:16,430 --> 00:01:18,220
All you do is cry!

3
00:01:18,250 --> 00:01:19,830
You can't learn a damn thing else!

4
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:21,330
If only you were this good at math!

5
00:01:21,330 --> 00:01:22,580
If you were so good at math,

6
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:24,200
our family would be rich thanks to you!

7
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:26,250
Shut up! Stop crying!

8
00:01:26,250 --> 00:01:26,950
Cry if you dare!

9
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:28,330
Mr. Wu!

10
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:29,870
Mr. Wu!

11
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:30,900
Quiet. Quiet.

12
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:40,450
Mrs. Huang, right? What's wrong?

13
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:42,580
I heard Dawei crying.

14
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:44,479
Just wanted to check on him.

15
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:49,039
[The 12th Thread]

16
00:01:49,060 --> 00:02:05,280
[Rewrite Our Life Scripts; At Least
We Learn to Lean on Each Other]

17
00:02:27,650 --> 00:02:31,010
[ATM]

18
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:30,810
Let me tell you,

19
00:02:31,090 --> 00:02:32,970
no matter how many times
you change your number,

20
00:02:32,970 --> 00:02:35,550
if I ask your mom, she'll still tell me.

21
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:38,050
It's useless. Don't be silly.

22
00:02:38,079 --> 00:02:39,210
Alright, that's it.

23
00:02:40,310 --> 00:02:42,250
Pick up when I call you from now on, okay?

24
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:43,579
Don't be so reluctant.

25
00:03:05,430 --> 00:03:07,050
Dawei. Dawei.

26
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:08,250
Dawei.

27
00:03:08,550 --> 00:03:09,880
Why were you in the rain?

28
00:03:15,290 --> 00:03:16,260
Let's go somewhere else.

29
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:17,340
Don't stay here.

30
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:26,480
It's fine.

31
00:03:26,510 --> 00:03:28,220
I just got a little wet.

32
00:03:28,329 --> 00:03:30,530
You don't have to worry about me so much.

33
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,950
I'm not worried about the wet.

34
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:38,000
Stop trying to be tough.

35
00:03:40,270 --> 00:03:41,500
Listen to me.

36
00:03:43,650 --> 00:03:44,890
From now on,

37
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:46,790
you're not alone.

38
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:48,460
I'll also try hard

39
00:03:48,540 --> 00:03:50,670
to be someone you can rely on.

40
00:03:52,320 --> 00:03:54,120
Whatever problems you face later,

41
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,579
we'll face them together.

42
00:03:56,870 --> 00:03:58,400
Are you willing to trust me?

43
00:04:06,330 --> 00:04:07,700
Then can you tell me

44
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:09,200
what happened?

45
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:15,560
If you can't say it, that's fine too.

46
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:18,940
I'll just see for myself.

47
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,450
What's the use of having a son like you?

48
00:04:26,450 --> 00:04:28,200
Do you know what trash is?

49
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,800
That's exactly what you are!

50
00:04:32,790 --> 00:04:34,590
What happened with your father?

51
00:04:35,730 --> 00:04:37,610
Are you very afraid of him?

52
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:41,330
Yeah.

53
00:04:43,650 --> 00:04:44,850
I'm terrified of him.

54
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:49,890
He beat me growing up,

55
00:04:51,110 --> 00:04:52,240
and my mom too.

56
00:04:54,950 --> 00:04:57,200
Later, my mom and I escaped that house,

57
00:04:57,700 --> 00:04:59,870
and my dad went around doing business,

58
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:02,150
so the nightmare finally ended.

59
00:05:05,570 --> 00:05:08,430
He just comes back from time to time
to ask for money.

60
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,490
Then for the past 3 years,

61
00:05:12,450 --> 00:05:15,080
my mom and I just completely
cut ties with him.

62
00:05:15,990 --> 00:05:19,120
The day before we were supposed to go
to the amusement park,

63
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,450
my dad suddenly called.

64
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:22,920
Since that day,

65
00:05:23,810 --> 00:05:25,410
the nightmare has returned.

66
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:27,300
So,

67
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:29,310
that heartless father

68
00:05:29,950 --> 00:05:32,210
is the reason
why Dawei's thread shattered.

69
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,880
[Psychic Club]

70
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:34,820
I think so.

71
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:40,970
I'm so mad.

72
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:44,100
When you meet a bad guy like that,
you just...

73
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:47,120
have to teach him a little lesson.

74
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,790
Like this, so he knows fear.

75
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:54,940
What kind of lesson do you think
we should teach him?

76
00:05:55,230 --> 00:05:57,380
I'm going to ask the Eight Lords
for a talisman

77
00:05:57,380 --> 00:05:58,690
to curse him.

78
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,780
Stop messing around.

79
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:01,770
You can't abuse the power
of the gods like this.

80
00:06:01,770 --> 00:06:03,140
I'm not abusing it.

81
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,470
The Eight Lords will definitely agree

82
00:06:04,470 --> 00:06:05,710
and grant my wish.

83
00:06:05,750 --> 00:06:07,080
I'm doing a good deed.

84
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:08,140
You need to know the difference.

85
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:09,620
Do you know, kid?

86
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:13,190
There's a clear line
between right and wrong.

87
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:16,880
[Psychic Club]

88
00:06:13,950 --> 00:06:14,550
What's up?

89
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:16,200
Okay, I'm heading over now.

90
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:17,000
What is it?

91
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:26,810
Dawei.

92
00:06:27,590 --> 00:06:28,420
Are you okay?

93
00:06:28,450 --> 00:06:29,620
Are you hurt?

94
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:32,070
Why are you here?

95
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:34,830
Zhiling told me you had
an incident on the road

96
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:36,370
and were in the hospital.

97
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:40,250
I just ran into a parked car on the road.

98
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:42,370
The driver wasn't feeling well,

99
00:06:42,370 --> 00:06:43,770
so I brought her to the ER.

100
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,920
So you're not hurt at all?

101
00:06:46,870 --> 00:06:47,950
Not a scratch.

102
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:51,040
Zhiling didn't explain it clearly.

103
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:52,420
I was worried sick.

104
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:54,200
Is that Jiakai?

105
00:06:57,860 --> 00:06:58,690
Ms. Peggy?

106
00:07:01,150 --> 00:07:02,660
Are you not feeling well?

107
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:05,760
I suddenly felt weak while driving.

108
00:07:06,190 --> 00:07:08,320
The police officer brought me here.

109
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,520
You guys know each other?

110
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:12,030
Why are you here?

111
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:13,190
What a coincidence.

112
00:07:14,370 --> 00:07:17,330
I'm here to see my police friend.

113
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:32,140
Ms. Peggy, are you pregnant?

114
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:38,020
You're asking for a beating.

115
00:07:39,940 --> 00:07:42,120
I only found out last week,

116
00:07:42,150 --> 00:07:43,550
and you saw it right away.

117
00:07:43,610 --> 00:07:44,810
You're amazing.

118
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:46,550
Sorry.

119
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:49,060
I'll keep it a secret for you, Ms. Peggy.

120
00:07:50,290 --> 00:07:53,040
I'm the one
who should be keeping a secret.

121
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:56,020
Your police officer.

122
00:07:57,250 --> 00:07:58,659
What do you mean?

123
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:03,490
Not bad.

124
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,800
He said he'd take me home.

125
00:08:07,330 --> 00:08:08,500
Impressive.

126
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:17,330
Officer, I'm sorry

127
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:19,470
to trouble you to drive my car
and take me back.

128
00:08:19,470 --> 00:08:21,410
I'll pay for your cab fare later.

129
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,760
It's fine.

130
00:08:22,780 --> 00:08:24,520
I'll just ask my colleague for help.

131
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:26,140
Don't be polite.

132
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:27,870
I'm going to make my husband pay for this.

133
00:08:27,870 --> 00:08:30,500
He actually dared
to ignore my calls just now.

134
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:33,830
Okay, thank you.

135
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:37,179
Jiakai just said

136
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:39,860
there's a white thread connecting
a mother and her baby.

137
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:41,120
I think it makes sense.

138
00:08:41,309 --> 00:08:43,559
White reminds people of new life

139
00:08:43,590 --> 00:08:45,040
and hope.

140
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,080
Could it be that

141
00:08:50,390 --> 00:08:52,890
not every baby's thread is white?

142
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:55,050
Because not everyone

143
00:08:55,070 --> 00:08:56,990
is born wanted.

144
00:09:02,070 --> 00:09:04,030
Whether a birth is wanted or not

145
00:09:04,050 --> 00:09:06,000
isn't the child's responsibility.

146
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,590
It's the parents' problem.

147
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:09,790
But they all have the ability

148
00:09:09,830 --> 00:09:12,580
to live a happy life full of expectations.

149
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:14,520
That's true.

150
00:09:16,330 --> 00:09:18,250
If you meet a child
who makes your heart ache in the future,

151
00:09:18,250 --> 00:09:20,700
you have to tell them this, okay?

152
00:09:30,490 --> 00:09:31,740
Where are we going?

153
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:34,700
To solve the problem once and for all.

154
00:09:34,830 --> 00:09:36,890
We're going to confront your father.

155
00:09:38,950 --> 00:09:40,150
You want to see my dad?

156
00:09:40,450 --> 00:09:42,580
I don't think talking to him will help.

157
00:09:42,830 --> 00:09:44,620
But hiding all day

158
00:09:44,650 --> 00:09:46,190
won't solve anything.

159
00:09:47,790 --> 00:09:48,840
Trust me.

160
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:52,590
Jiakai.

161
00:09:52,890 --> 00:09:54,500
[Public Welfare Lottery]

162
00:09:59,770 --> 00:10:01,370
Make it clear to your father.

163
00:10:08,150 --> 00:10:09,280
Why are you here?

164
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,580
Alright, it's fine. Come here.

165
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:13,500
I'm really unlucky.

166
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,390
Over 5,000 New Taiwan dollars,
and not a single winning ticket.

167
00:10:15,390 --> 00:10:16,390
Come on, hurry up.

168
00:10:16,420 --> 00:10:18,370
A few thousand, 2 thousand.
Just give me whatever you have.

169
00:10:18,370 --> 00:10:19,120
Hurry up, move it.

170
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,080
Mr. Wu.

171
00:10:20,470 --> 00:10:22,090
Just say how much you want.

172
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:24,750
Don't think you can just take
whatever you want.

173
00:10:22,820 --> 00:10:24,930
[Public Welfare Lottery]

174
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:25,830
Who are you?

175
00:10:26,370 --> 00:10:27,220
I'm the one...

176
00:10:28,190 --> 00:10:29,650
negotiating for Dawei.

177
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:31,870
Negotiating?

178
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:33,530
I think you...

179
00:10:37,070 --> 00:10:38,120
Why did you hit him?

180
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:40,080
Do I need to report to you
when I hit someone?

181
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:41,450
I'll beat you!

182
00:10:44,250 --> 00:10:45,310
What are you doing?

183
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:46,610
Let me go!

184
00:10:47,110 --> 00:10:48,050
Let me go!

185
00:10:48,470 --> 00:10:49,400
What do you want?

186
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:50,170
Let me go!

187
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:52,980
You think you're tough now, huh?

188
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:54,150
Let me go!

189
00:10:54,370 --> 00:10:55,870
I used to be unable to protect myself

190
00:10:55,870 --> 00:10:56,950
and Mom.

191
00:10:58,150 --> 00:11:00,750
Now I won't let you hurt
the people I care about!

192
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,930
You've grown up, haven't you?

193
00:11:02,930 --> 00:11:05,010
Let me go, you little brat!

194
00:11:05,490 --> 00:11:08,040
You're nothing to me!

195
00:11:11,370 --> 00:11:13,000
I have my own life to live!

196
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,500
It's broken! Let go! Let go!

197
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:16,430
You want to live like this forever?

198
00:11:17,470 --> 00:11:18,330
Suit yourself.

199
00:11:29,870 --> 00:11:31,750
You laid a hand on your own dad?

200
00:11:32,250 --> 00:11:34,250
I'll teach you a lesson another day!

201
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:35,850
This isn't over!

202
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:42,360
Are you okay?

203
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:43,700
Are you hurt?

204
00:11:44,330 --> 00:11:45,500
I'm fine.

205
00:11:58,700 --> 00:11:59,820
You're fine too.

206
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:34,170
Hello?

207
00:12:34,780 --> 00:12:35,480
Hello.

208
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:36,740
Mom.

209
00:12:38,830 --> 00:12:39,730
Are you busy?

210
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:43,080
I was just about to call you.

211
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:45,920
Before that guy went abroad,

212
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,920
he said he was going to see your aunt.

213
00:12:48,780 --> 00:12:50,280
To borrow money, right?

214
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:53,000
Aunt told me this afternoon.

215
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:56,720
Are things okay on your end?

216
00:12:57,870 --> 00:12:58,560
It's fine.

217
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:01,470
Don't worry.

218
00:13:04,370 --> 00:13:07,630
This seems to be the first time
you've called me on your own.

219
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:11,540
Perfect timing.

220
00:13:15,310 --> 00:13:17,740
Happy birthday, my son.

221
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:25,300
This seems to be

222
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:29,930
the first time you've wished me
a happy birthday.

223
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:32,000
How is that possible?

224
00:13:33,610 --> 00:13:34,480
Yeah.

225
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:39,760
Because you guys never
celebrated my birthday.

226
00:13:40,970 --> 00:13:42,890
So I thought you always hated me.

227
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,230
I'm sorry.

228
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:56,070
I was too weak. I didn't protect you well.

229
00:13:57,370 --> 00:13:58,620
I'm sorry.

230
00:14:06,780 --> 00:14:09,430
I've always been grateful
to have you as my son.

231
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:21,560
Thank you for letting me know

232
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,570
you don't regret having me.

233
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:32,290
See you next time then.

234
00:14:48,370 --> 00:14:51,850
[Police]

235
00:14:53,370 --> 00:14:55,950
Anyway, our New Year's Eve event this year

236
00:14:55,950 --> 00:14:58,210
will be extended by one hour on both ends.

237
00:14:58,370 --> 00:15:00,450
So, for those on the late-night

238
00:15:00,450 --> 00:15:02,120
New Year's Eve shift tonight,

239
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:04,450
please work a little harder, okay?

240
00:15:04,450 --> 00:15:05,580
-Got it.
-Got it.

241
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:09,860
This light‑blocking effect is really good.

242
00:15:09,870 --> 00:15:11,870
I definitely bought the right pair.

243
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:27,240
Hello?

244
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:28,520
Jiakai.

245
00:15:28,770 --> 00:15:31,020
Happy New Year!

246
00:15:31,940 --> 00:15:33,020
Happy New Year.

247
00:15:33,050 --> 00:15:35,110
Happy New Year. Guess what I'm doing.

248
00:15:35,980 --> 00:15:37,040
What are you doing?

249
00:15:37,870 --> 00:15:39,910
I'm at a B&B with Yujing

250
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:41,390
and the juniors from the club.

251
00:15:41,390 --> 00:15:43,390
We bought a ton of alcohol,

252
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:44,950
including sorghum, beer, and sake.

253
00:15:44,950 --> 00:15:46,930
I'm going to mix them
and get them wasted!

254
00:15:46,930 --> 00:15:48,300
So passionate.

255
00:15:49,080 --> 00:15:50,740
You guys are drinking so much.

256
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:52,390
Be careful not to throw up.

257
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:55,020
It's a pity, I know.

258
00:15:55,050 --> 00:15:56,340
Your boyfriend

259
00:15:56,370 --> 00:15:58,080
has the responsibility
of protecting the citizens.

260
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:59,520
He can't just take care of you,

261
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:00,580
right?

262
00:16:01,890 --> 00:16:02,760
No.

263
00:16:03,710 --> 00:16:05,710
Actually, I'm quite used to it now.

264
00:16:05,730 --> 00:16:06,850
Come on.

265
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,140
Didn't you buy a bunch of sunglasses

266
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:09,200
for New Year's Eve?

267
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:11,450
Not a bunch,

268
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:14,080
just 2 pairs.

269
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:16,100
Hilarious.

270
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:17,440
Speaking of your boyfriend,

271
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:19,370
is his father still bothering him?

272
00:16:21,010 --> 00:16:22,620
Dawei said last time

273
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:24,570
that he seemed to have gone abroad.

274
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:26,830
After what happened before,

275
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:29,260
he probably wouldn't dare
to show up again.

276
00:16:30,550 --> 00:16:31,130
Wait a minute.

277
00:16:31,130 --> 00:16:31,930
Wait a minute.

278
00:16:31,950 --> 00:16:33,250
Let me go check on those brats.

279
00:16:33,250 --> 00:16:34,450
That beer is mine.

280
00:16:34,450 --> 00:16:35,580
Don't drink it!

281
00:16:36,250 --> 00:16:37,540
You're the brat.

282
00:16:38,370 --> 00:16:40,000
Why did you call me anyway?

283
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:47,290
Zhiling.

284
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:48,580
Jiakai.

285
00:16:48,830 --> 00:16:50,500
Why are you wearing sunglasses?

286
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:52,750
Because there are a lot of people today,

287
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:54,580
and the threads will be glaring.

288
00:16:54,710 --> 00:16:55,490
Well,

289
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:57,080
why are you here?

290
00:16:57,330 --> 00:16:59,390
Isn't this where Dawei is on duty?

291
00:16:59,830 --> 00:17:01,370
Dawei swapped shifts with me
a long time ago.

292
00:17:01,370 --> 00:17:03,700
He's on duty tomorrow. Didn't he tell you?

293
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:05,650
Let me ask him.

294
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:08,000
Hey, Dawei.

295
00:17:08,329 --> 00:17:09,579
Where are you?

296
00:17:09,950 --> 00:17:10,910
I'm on duty.

297
00:17:10,910 --> 00:17:11,730
On duty?

298
00:17:11,750 --> 00:17:12,950
But here...

299
00:17:13,579 --> 00:17:14,640
I'm busy right now.

300
00:17:17,450 --> 00:17:18,369
Bye-bye.

301
00:17:20,750 --> 00:17:22,150
What are you laughing at?

302
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:25,900
You still don't get it?

303
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,580
Dawei wants to surprise you.

304
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:30,710
That's why he lied about being on duty.

305
00:17:30,830 --> 00:17:31,710
Really?

306
00:17:31,890 --> 00:17:32,760
What else?

307
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:35,280
Would you prefer him cheating on you?

308
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:36,480
No.

309
00:17:36,510 --> 00:17:37,510
Exactly.

310
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:41,140
Why don't you go find him?
Are you just going to space out?

311
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:42,740
How am I supposed to find him?

312
00:17:43,550 --> 00:17:46,410
Take off your sunglasses.
Can't you see his thread?

313
00:17:48,090 --> 00:17:49,010
Bye-bye.

314
00:17:54,070 --> 00:17:54,950
Dawei!

315
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:06,800
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

316
00:19:00,330 --> 00:19:01,450
That's weird.

317
00:19:01,710 --> 00:19:03,170
He was right here.

318
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:15,210
Stop hiding.

319
00:19:25,230 --> 00:19:27,190
I knew you'd find me.

320
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:29,980
And I knew you'd be waiting for me.

321
00:19:39,130 --> 00:19:40,160
Am I heavy?

322
00:19:40,190 --> 00:19:41,220
No.

323
00:19:44,170 --> 00:19:46,250
Do you know why I brought you here?

324
00:19:50,060 --> 00:19:51,010
Why?

325
00:19:52,340 --> 00:19:54,170
You'll see in a minute.

326
00:19:59,310 --> 00:20:00,140
Alright.

327
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:02,920
You can open your eyes now.

328
00:20:08,930 --> 00:20:10,930
Do you remember where this is?

329
00:20:12,150 --> 00:20:13,740
Isn't this where you

330
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:16,460
first thought I was a pervert?

331
00:20:17,830 --> 00:20:18,660
Yes.

332
00:20:25,450 --> 00:20:27,180
Should we start the countdown?

333
00:20:30,420 --> 00:20:31,500
-Seven.
-Seven.

334
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:32,690
-Six.
-Six.

335
00:20:32,730 --> 00:20:33,530
-Five.
-Five.

336
00:20:33,820 --> 00:20:34,680
-Four.
-Four.

337
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:35,770
-Three.
-Three.

338
00:20:36,140 --> 00:20:36,950
-Two.
-Two.

339
00:20:37,330 --> 00:20:37,990
-One.
-One.

340
00:20:42,450 --> 00:20:43,290
Wow.

341
00:20:43,380 --> 00:20:44,570
Look at that.

342
00:20:45,340 --> 00:20:46,400
It's so beautiful.

343
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:51,680
I used to think

344
00:20:52,410 --> 00:20:53,870
the person connected to me

345
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:56,740
would never appear.

346
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,270
Until I met Dawei,

347
00:21:01,020 --> 00:21:02,440
who made me believe that

348
00:21:03,250 --> 00:21:04,910
there is someone in this world

349
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:06,710
who will understand you,

350
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:07,940
find you,

351
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:10,260
and connect with you.

352
00:21:42,090 --> 00:21:44,590
[Peggy Talks Love Psychology]

353
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,700
So many people are online today.

354
00:21:44,700 --> 00:21:45,950
Two-Minute Love Live Stream.

355
00:21:44,930 --> 00:21:45,840
[Two-Minute Love Live Stream]

356
00:21:45,950 --> 00:21:47,620
It's fleeting, so don't miss it.

357
00:21:47,620 --> 00:21:49,120
I'm Ms. Peggy.

358
00:21:49,120 --> 00:21:49,990
I saw someone

359
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:51,200
leave a comment right away today.

360
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,450
Let me read it.

361
00:21:52,620 --> 00:21:54,330
I really want to be pampered,

362
00:21:54,330 --> 00:21:56,830
but I always end up dating mama's boys.

363
00:21:56,830 --> 00:21:57,960
I'm always the one taking care of them.

364
00:21:57,960 --> 00:22:00,080
Damn, did I bring this upon myself?

365
00:22:00,620 --> 00:22:01,390
Okay,

366
00:22:01,410 --> 00:22:01,830
well,

367
00:22:01,830 --> 00:22:02,870
for you,

368
00:22:02,870 --> 00:22:04,190
I'll talk about

369
00:22:04,210 --> 00:22:05,580
life script today.

370
00:22:05,600 --> 00:22:07,080
Life Script.

371
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:07,580
This

372
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:08,950
was proposed by an American psychologist

373
00:22:08,950 --> 00:22:09,490
named

374
00:22:09,510 --> 00:22:10,190
Eric

375
00:22:10,220 --> 00:22:11,080
Berne.

376
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:12,200
It means that

377
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:13,620
as we grow up,

378
00:22:13,620 --> 00:22:14,410
we create

379
00:22:14,430 --> 00:22:15,330
our own life scripts

380
00:22:15,330 --> 00:22:17,330
based on early experiences,

381
00:22:17,330 --> 00:22:19,580
thinking this is how we
will spend our lives.

382
00:22:19,580 --> 00:22:20,830
Of course, there are positive ones too.

383
00:22:20,830 --> 00:22:21,790
Let me give you an example.

384
00:22:21,790 --> 00:22:22,490
Well,

385
00:22:22,520 --> 00:22:23,320
you said

386
00:22:23,350 --> 00:22:25,540
you wanted to be pampered,

387
00:22:25,570 --> 00:22:27,590
but ended up taking care of others.

388
00:22:27,610 --> 00:22:28,470
Could it be that

389
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:29,370
in your life script,

390
00:22:29,370 --> 00:22:30,730
you set it up so that

391
00:22:30,750 --> 00:22:31,750
if you don't give

392
00:22:31,750 --> 00:22:32,730
or work hard,

393
00:22:32,750 --> 00:22:34,080
you don't deserve to be loved?

394
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:35,950
I think this is worth thinking about.

395
00:22:35,950 --> 00:22:37,950
We often hear some parents say,

396
00:22:37,950 --> 00:22:39,450
"Yes, it's because of you

397
00:22:39,450 --> 00:22:40,830
that our family is so poor."

398
00:22:40,830 --> 00:22:41,700
Such children

399
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:42,990
might grow up feeling

400
00:22:43,020 --> 00:22:44,950
they don't deserve happiness.

401
00:22:44,950 --> 00:22:46,590
Or some people might say,

402
00:22:47,310 --> 00:22:49,200
"Who would love you looking like that?"

403
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:50,110
Such children

404
00:22:50,130 --> 00:22:51,000
might grow up

405
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:53,120
feeling they are unworthy of love.

406
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:54,870
Many people in interpersonal

407
00:22:54,330 --> 00:22:55,360
[Interpersonal Relationships]

408
00:22:54,870 --> 00:22:56,200
or romantic relationships

409
00:22:55,360 --> 00:22:57,370
[Interpersonal Relationships]
[Romantic Relationships]

410
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:57,580
often wonder

411
00:22:57,580 --> 00:22:59,080
why they keep encountering

412
00:22:59,080 --> 00:22:59,450
situations

413
00:22:59,450 --> 00:23:00,870
where others mistreat them.

414
00:23:00,870 --> 00:23:02,600
And it keeps repeating,

415
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:03,450
unable to change.

416
00:23:03,450 --> 00:23:04,420
Perhaps,

417
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:06,370
it's because our life script is set

418
00:23:06,370 --> 00:23:08,250
so that we can't consistently

419
00:23:08,250 --> 00:23:11,450
receive such care and love
in a positive way.

420
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:11,530
[Inner Insecurity]

421
00:23:11,450 --> 00:23:12,330
Although

422
00:23:12,350 --> 00:23:13,450
life scripts might have been

423
00:23:13,450 --> 00:23:15,080
written when we were young,

424
00:23:15,080 --> 00:23:15,620
we

425
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:16,690
don't need to be bound

426
00:23:16,690 --> 00:23:18,500
by these shackles.

427
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:20,500
Everyone's life script

428
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:22,330
can be rewritten

429
00:23:22,350 --> 00:23:24,580
starting from now.

430
00:23:24,830 --> 00:23:26,620
I also wish this student well.

431
00:23:26,620 --> 00:23:27,090
May you

432
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:28,500
not encounter mama's boys anymore.

433
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:29,260
Or if you do

434
00:23:29,290 --> 00:23:31,620
encounter someone
you think is a mama's boy,

435
00:23:31,620 --> 00:23:33,080
you can turn things around

436
00:23:33,080 --> 00:23:35,750
and make him pamper you too.

437
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:37,950
Alright,

438
00:23:37,950 --> 00:23:38,870
that's it for today.

439
00:23:38,870 --> 00:23:39,780
Bye-bye.
